# R Testing Rules

## testthat 3rd Edition
Every test file starts with `local_edition(3)`. Use `withr` package for temporary state (files, options, environment variables).

## Test Organization
One test file per `R/` source file: `R/features.R` → `tests/testthat/test-features.R`. Function names match: test for `compute_ratio()` is in a block `test_that("compute_ratio handles NA", {...})`.

## Fixture Data
Test fixtures live in `tests/testthat/fixtures/` or `data/fixtures/`. Use `readr::read_csv(testthat::test_path("fixtures/sample.csv"))`. Never hardcode absolute paths.

## What to Test
- Happy path: expected transformation with fixture data
- Edge cases: empty data frame, NA values, zero-row input
- Error cases: `expect_error(fn(bad_input), class = "my_error_class")`
- Snapshot tests: `expect_snapshot(print(complex_object))` for outputs that are hard to assert structurally

## What NOT to Test
- ggplot2 visual output (use snapshot tests only if visual regression matters)
- Quarto rendering (test the functions, not the document)
- External API calls (mock with httptest2)

## Coverage Target
`covr::package_coverage()` on the `R/` directory. Target: > 80% line coverage on `R/` functions.
